    "dynamic_instructions": "{\r\n  \"datasetView\": \"**Train Tree 1**\\n\\nGoal: Train your model and test it for your user.\\n\\n1. In **Predict**, choose the label from **My Data** in your guide.\\n2. In **Using**, choose only the two features you put on your map in Define Stop 3. Write them in **Tree 1** in your guide.\\n3. Click **Train model**.\\n\\nYou are done when your tree shows. Go to the **Testing** tab.\",\r\n  \"results\": \"**Train Tree 1**\\n\\nGoal: Train your model and test it for your user.\\n\\n1. Find your **Accuracy** at the top. Write it in **Tree 1** in your guide.\\n2. Click **Accuracy**. Write the **Correct** number in **Tree 1**.\\n3. Add **Correct** and **Incorrect**. Write the total after \\\"out of\\\". Click **Back to Testing**.\\n4. Write your user from Define Stop 2 on the **My user** line in **Tree 1**.\\n5. In **Make a Prediction**, choose a category for each feature that fits your user. Write them in the **My user** table.\\n6. Click **Predict**. Wait until the path stops moving. Write the prediction in **Tree 1**.\\n7. Click **Save image** (the camera under your tree). Click **Save to Backpack**.\\n\\nYou are done when **Tree 1** in your guide is full and your tree is in your Backpack.\\n\\nThink about: Which of your two features did your tree ask about? Why?\"\r\n}",
